---
import Policy from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
---

<Policy
  title="Privacy Policy | India Visit"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  description="How India Visit collects, uses and protects the personal information you share when enquiring about a journey."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    The information you give us when you enquire — name, phone or WhatsApp
    number, email address, the destination and month you have in mind, and
    anything you choose to tell us about the trip. We also collect standard
    analytics about how the site is used.
  </p>

  <h2 id="why">Why we collect it</h2>
  <p>
    To answer your enquiry and plan your journey, and to improve the site.
    Nothing more. The section your lawyer will want to expand here is the
    lawful basis for each purpose.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sharing">Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    Suppliers who need it to deliver your trip — hotels, transport operators,
    guides, and train operators where a booking requires it — and the services
    that run this site's forms and email. This section must name them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>To be confirmed by the client's legal adviser.</p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Your rights of access, correction, erasure and grievance redress under
    India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023, and — for travellers
    enquiring from the EU and UK — under the GDPR. This section must name the
    grievance officer and how to reach them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Which tags run, what they store, and how a visitor declines them. This site
    loads its tags through Google Tag Manager, so this section has to be kept in
    step with whatever is configured there.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contacting us</h2>
  <p>The contact details in the footer reach us for any question about this policy.</p>
</Policy>
